>
> For missiles I will at least have a stack of blessed +5/6
> elven daggers even for a class that can't enhance dagger
> skill.  But classes that can use bow there's the launcher,
> more than one type of arrow.  And any silver daggers ever
> found.

The stack of daggers (or a stack of arrows for bow-users) makes
sense.  Multiple kinds of arrows, meh.  Unless I find a ton of elvish
arrows meybe.
The launcher, not so much.  With maxed luck you're never going to miss
anyway, and it doesn't help damage--so basically, it's worthless once
luck is maxed.  Odds of getting enough scrolls to do my melee weapon
and a stack of arrows and still have some for the launcher _before_
maxing luck are really small for me.
The silver daggers I wouldn't bother with unless I got a stack of 4+
(yet to happen).

> For melee I don't hesitate to enchant early non-artifact
> ones and build skills in assorted types.

If I find a b?enchant weapon early I'll use it on the best available
weapon (even a "disposable" non-artifact).
I'm not sure why you'd do several of those, though (no real reason to
amass lots of melee skills).

> For artifacts I'll enchant Sunsword just because I might
> want to use it in the swamp levels deep down.  For the
> main chosen melee artifact like Exc/Grey/Storm/etc I
> will be carrying it most of the game so it makes sense.
> A class that can #twoweapon that ends up an artifact
> and a non-artifact dual wielded.  A class that can't that
> ends up two different types of artifact to "x" between.
> Maybe Magicbane and Stormy, or Greyswandir and
> Sunsword, or whatever happened to arrive in the game.

Grayswandir+Magicbane would make some sense.  Sunsword I'll wield but
won't enchant (just switch if I need stopping power).

I rarely wind up with more than one decent artifact, though; once I
have one I stop sac'ing (why waste time?).  But sometimes I'll hit a
bones pile or find one randomly gen'd or something (or get sunsword
from an angel-type).

> For the rest of artifacts I tend to enchant them because
> the scrolls are there.  Style issue.

If you have tons, sure.  But it seems like if you're going to carry a
pickaxe, it's more useful to enchant that before you start enchanting
random artifact weapons.


